# Break-glass basic-auth for oauth2-proxy (fallback when GitHub is unavailable, or
# for a non-GitHub operator). Copy to `htpasswd` (gitignored) and add bcrypt entries:
#
#   htpasswd -B -c deploy/oauth/htpasswd insight       # first user (prompts for pw)
#   htpasswd -B    deploy/oauth/htpasswd someoneelse   # more users
#
# Then set in .env:  OAUTH_HTPASSWD_FILE=/etc/oauth2-proxy/htpasswd
# oauth2-proxy accepts requests carrying matching HTTP Basic credentials and skips
# the GitHub flow for them. Keep this file OUT of git (it holds password hashes).
insight:$2y$05$REPLACE_WITH_A_REAL_BCRYPT_HASH..........................
